{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Close attempt blocked — escalating to a human operator rather than bypassing the gate.\n\n`transition_ticket(open -> closed, close_class=\"superseded\")` was refused:\n\n```\nplan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation.\nRun rebar review-plan a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711 separately, then retry close.\n```\n\n`plan_review_status` confirms `verdict: unsigned` — this ticket has no signature at all, and its `plan_review_phase` is still `planning`: it never passed plan review, because it was decomposed into epic 87d8's 11 slices instead of being executed. The completion precheck the close would otherwise have hit is already satisfied: `declare_no_file_impact` was recorded above, replacing the ~40 stale `file_impact` entries.\n\nTwo non-bypass paths remain, both human calls:\n\n1. Run `review-plan` on this superseded monolithic plan to earn the attestation, then close. That spends a 15-20 minute LLM gate on a plan that is deliberately obsolete, and a PASS is not assured.\n2. A human operator closes with the documented `--force=<reason>` break-glass, which records the absent attestation as the audit signal.\n\nAgents must not run force overrides, so this ticket stays `open` pending that decision. Parent epic `87d8-8bb6` cannot close until this resolves."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793379722331631106,"uuid":"d834c116-e578-4427-92e4-9b44a7ca23b9"}